# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0

config MESHTASTIC_DIAG_LOOP_STACK_SIZE
	int "Stack size for the combined thread-summary/supervisor diagnostic loop"
	default 2048
	depends on MESHTASTIC_THREAD_SUMMARY || MESHTASTIC_SUPERVISOR
	help
	  agents-wu94.12.1: mt_thread_summary (was CONFIG_MESHTASTIC_THREAD_SUMMARY_STACK_SIZE,
	  2048 B) and mt_supervisor_thread (was CONFIG_MESHTASTIC_SUPERVISOR_STACK_SIZE,
	  4096 B) merged onto one thread with one stack, replacing both symbols with
	  this one. 2026-09-19 soak (0.3.53, courier + class-4, 2-4 h uptime) measured
	  the two SEPARATE stacks peaking at 1028-1060/2048 B (50-52%) and 852-916/4096 B
	  (21-22%) respectively -- 2048 B covers both observed peaks with real margin,
	  not a computed minimum from that one short sample (the standing rule from
	  agents-wu94.8). Re-measure on the merged thread's own high-water mark before
	  trusting this number on hardware; a scheduling-coupling regression (a delayed
	  sweep, not a stack overflow) is the risk this merge trades in, per the parent
	  bead's soak requirement.

	  Linked DRAM delta measured on a class-2-style build (heltec_wifi_lora32_v4_r8,
	  overlay-cluster-sign.conf, otherwise stock samples/meshtastic/prj.conf): dram0_0_seg
	  150048 B before this merge, 145808 B after -- 4240 B reclaimed, ahead of the ~4 KB
	  estimate from stack sizes alone. Still outstanding before fleet rollout: flash ONE
	  node, soak a full multi-day cycle, and provoke both alert paths (a heap-low WARN and
	  a stack/cpu WARN) at least once before trusting the merged thread's own high-water
	  mark on real hardware.
